                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "To determine what happens if someone kisses too long, we need to consider the physiological and emotional effects of kissing, as well as potential risks associated with prolonged kissing.\n\nHelpful knowledge and important additional facts:\n1. Kissing involves the exchange of saliva, which can transmit bacteria and viruses.\n2. Kissing can lead to the release of hormones and neurotransmitters, such as oxytocin and dopamine, which are associated with feelings of attachment, pleasure, and reward.\n3. Prolonged kissing can lead to increased heart rate and blood flow, which can cause feelings of excitement and arousal.\n4. Kissing for an extended period without taking breaks to breathe can lead to shortness of breath.\n\nSub-questions and answers:\n1. Can prolonged kissing lead to strong feelings?\nYes, the release of hormones and neurotransmitters during kissing can lead to strong feelings of attachment and pleasure.\n\n2. Can prolonged kissing transmit herpes?\nYes, if one person has an active herpes outbreak (cold sore), prolonged kissing can increase the risk of transmitting the herpes virus to the other person.\n\n3. Can prolonged kissing cause shortness of breath?\nYes, if the individuals do not take breaks to breathe during the prolonged kissing, they may experience shortness of breath.\n\n4. Can prolonged kissing lead to excitement and arousal?\nYes, the increased heart rate and blood flow during prolonged kissing can lead to feelings of excitement and arousal.\n\nBased on the reasoning above, the answer to the original question is:\nWhat happens if someone kisses too long?\nA) strong feelings\nB) herpes (if one person has an active outbreak)\nC) shortness of breath\nD) excitement\nE) arousal",
