 path. In a quarry, stones are extracted and not arranged in any specific way, whereas in a bridge, stones could be arranged in a specific way to support the structure. So, the best answer would be option A, quarries.\n\nStudent: That makes sense. Thank you for helping me work through the question step by step. I understand it much better now.\n\nProfessor: You're welcome!",
