                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Professor, I'm not sure how to answer this question about knitting and using a radio. Can you help me work it out?\n\nProfessor: Of course! Let's look at the options one by one. First, can you watch television while knitting and using a radio?\n\nStudent: No, because a radio is for listening, not watching.\n\nProfessor: Correct. So that eliminates options B and E. Now, can you make blankets while knitting and using a radio?\n\nStudent: Well, you can make blankets by knitting, but that doesn't have anything to do with the radio.\n\nProfessor: Exactly. So that eliminates option C. What about eating while knitting and using a radio?\n\nStudent: I guess you could eat while knitting and listening to the radio, but it might be difficult to do all three at the same time.\n\nProfessor: True, but the question is asking what you \"can\" do, not what is easy to do. So, we can't eliminate option D yet. Finally, can you listen to music while knitting and using a radio?\n\nStudent: Yes, you can listen to music on the radio while knitting.\n\nProfessor: Great! So now we have two options left: A) listen to music and D) eat. Which one do you think is the best answer?\n\nStudent: I think A) listen to music is the best answer because it's more directly related to using a radio.\n\nProfessor: I agree. So the correct answer is A) listen to music. Do you understand how we worked that out?\n\nStudent: Yes, thank you for helping me go through the options step by step. It makes more sense now.",
