                    {
                        "id": "1b654ecf-a7bd-4871-b131-a5927190c367",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-12",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "When you travel, you should consider the possibility of unexpected costs. To prepare for this, it is important to have a plan in place. Here is a step-by-step breakdown of the thought process and reasoning behind the correct answer:\n\n1. Analyze the question: The question is asking what you should do when traveling to be prepared for unexpected costs.\n\n2. Evaluate the answer choices:\n\nA) Go somewhere: This choice does not address the issue of unexpected costs. It is simply stating an action related to traveling.\n\nB) Energy: This choice is unrelated to the topic of unexpected costs during travel.\n\nC) Spend frivolously: This choice is counterproductive, as spending frivolously would likely lead to more unexpected costs and financial strain.\n\nD) Fly in airplane: This choice is also unrelated to the topic of unexpected costs. It is simply stating a mode of transportation.\n\nE) Have money: This choice addresses the issue of unexpected costs by suggesting that you should have money available to cover any unforeseen expenses during your travels.\n\n3. Choose the correct answer: Based on the evaluation of the answer choices, the correct answer is E) have money. This is because having money available will allow you to be prepared for any unexpected costs that may arise during your travels.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "026aece2-bb97-43fc-91b3-466c45efc50b",
