                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Professor, I'm not sure how to answer this question about what to do when traveling in case of unexpected costs. Can you help me work it out?\n\nProfessor: Of course! Let's go through the options one by one. Option A says \"go somewhere.\" Does that make sense in the context of unexpected costs?\n\nStudent: No, not really. That doesn't seem to address the issue of unexpected costs.\n\nProfessor: Right. Let's move on to option B, \"energy.\" Does that have anything to do with unexpected costs while traveling?\n\nStudent: No, I don't think so.\n\nProfessor: Agreed. Now, option C is \"spend frivolously.\" What do you think about that one?\n\nStudent: That seems like the opposite of what we should do in case of unexpected costs.\n\nProfessor: Exactly. So we can eliminate that option as well. Option D is \"fly in an airplane.\" Does that help with unexpected costs?\n\nStudent: No, that's just a mode of transportation. It doesn't really address the issue.\n\nProfessor: Correct. Finally, we have option E, \"have money.\" How does that relate to unexpected costs?\n\nStudent: Well, if you have money set aside, you'll be able to handle any unexpected costs that come up while traveling.\n\nProfessor: That's right! So, which option do you think is the correct answer?\n\nStudent: I think the correct answer is E, \"have money.\"\n\nProfessor: Great job! You've worked through the options and arrived at the correct answer. Do you feel confident in your understanding of how we got there?\n\nStudent: Yes, thank you for helping me work through it step by step, Professor!",
