                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nThe correct answer is E) have money.\n\nWhen traveling, it is important to have money in case of unexpected costs. Unexpected costs can include anything from an emergency medical expense to an unexpected flight delay or cancellation. Having money on hand can help you cover these costs without having to worry about how you will pay for them. Additionally, having money can help you cover any additional costs that may arise, such as food, lodging, or transportation. Having money can also help you take advantage of any unexpected opportunities that may arise, such as a discounted flight or a last-minute hotel deal. Therefore, the best way to prepare for unexpected costs while traveling is to have money.",
