                        "cot": "Running errands with screaming kids will likely cause:\n\nStep 1: Analyze each option in relation to the situation.\n\nA) Efficiency - This is unlikely, as screaming kids can be distracting and make it difficult to focus on completing tasks efficiently.\n\nB) Insanity - This is an extreme outcome and not a direct result of the situation.\n\nC) Aggravation - This is a possible outcome, as screaming kids can be frustrating and cause irritation.\n\nD) Tiredness - This is also a possible outcome, as dealing with screaming kids can be physically and mentally exhausting.\n\nE) Stress - This is another possible outcome, as managing screaming kids while trying to complete errands can be stressful.\n\nStep 2: Determine the most likely outcome.\n\nOut of the three possible outcomes (C, D, and E), the most likely outcome is:\n\nE) Stress - Running errands with screaming kids will likely cause stress, as it can be challenging to manage their behavior while trying to complete tasks.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "03dc9262-57dc-4730-ba81-a8401832c765",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-E",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "E) Stress.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "E",
                                "correct_answer": false
                            }
                        ],
                        "author": "thoughtsource",
                        "date": "2023/04/12 19:01:52",
                        "api_service": "openai_chat",
