                        "instruction": "qa-13",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "First, let's rephrase the question to ensure we understand it correctly: What is the probable outcome of running errands with screaming children?\n\nNow, let's work this out step by step, spelling out our thoughts and reasoning:\n\nA) Efficiency - It is unlikely that having screaming kids while running errands would make the process more efficient.\nB) Insanity - While it might feel overwhelming, it is not likely to cause actual insanity.\nC) Aggravation - This seems like a plausible outcome, as screaming kids can be frustrating and make errands more difficult.\nD) Tiredness - This could be a possible outcome, as dealing with screaming kids can be exhausting.\nE) Stress - This is also a plausible outcome, as managing screaming kids while trying to complete errands can be stressful.\n\nAfter evaluating each option, we can conclude that the most likely outcomes are aggravation and stress. However, since we need to choose one answer, we should consider which one is more directly related to the situation. In this case, stress seems to be the more encompassing term, as it can include both aggravation and tiredness.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is E) stress.",
                        "answers": [
