                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "To answer this question, we need to consider the appropriate attitude for a funeral and which of the given options best fits that description.\n\nA funeral is a ceremony for honoring, remembering, and celebrating the life of a deceased person. It is a time for family and friends to come together and support each other in their grief. Therefore, the appropriate attitude for a funeral should be respectful, empathetic, and considerate of the feelings of others.\n\nNow, let's evaluate each of the given options:\n\nA) Straightforward - This attitude implies being honest and direct, which can be appropriate in some situations, but it does not necessarily convey the emotional sensitivity needed at a funeral.\n\nB) Serious - This attitude suggests being focused and not taking things lightly, which is more fitting for a funeral than being straightforward. However, it may not fully capture the emotional depth of the situation.\n\nC) Solemn - This attitude conveys a sense of deep sincerity and gravity, which is highly appropriate for a funeral. It shows respect for the deceased and empathy for the grieving family and friends.\n\nD) Somber - This attitude implies a feeling of sadness and seriousness, which is also fitting for a funeral. However, it may not convey the same level of emotional depth and respect as being solemn.\n\nE) Funny - This attitude is clearly inappropriate for a funeral, as it does not show respect for the deceased or consideration for the feelings of others.\n\nBased on this analysis, the man should have taken a solemn (C) attitude at the funeral, as it best conveys the respect, empathy, and emotional sensitivity needed in such a situation.",
