                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Professor, can you explain this question to me?\n\nProfessor: Sure, what do you need help with?\n\nStudent: I don't understand what the question is asking. Can you explain it to me?\n\nProfessor: Of course. The question is asking what the little boy's response was when his mother asked him why he did something.\n\nStudent: Oh, I see. So, the little boy didn't know why he did it?\n\nProfessor: Yes, that's correct.\n\nStudent: Okay, and the question is asking what his response was?\n\nProfessor: Exactly. Now, the answer choices are A) case, B) reason, C) how, D) because, and E) answer. Which one do you think is the correct answer?\n\nStudent: Hmm, I'm not sure. Can you explain each option to me?\n\nProfessor: Sure. A) case doesn't really make sense in this context. B) reason could work, but it's not the best option. C) how doesn't fit either. D) because is a possibility, but it's not the best answer. E) answer is the correct choice because it directly relates to the question being asked.\n\nStudent: Oh, I understand now. Thank you for explaining it to me step by step.\n\nProfessor: You're welcome. It's important to break down the question and answer choices to fully understand what's being asked.",
