                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "To answer this question, we need to understand the context and find the most appropriate word to complete the sentence. The sentence is:\n\nShe asked her little boy why, he replied that he didn't know and it was just ___.\n\nNow let's analyze each option:\n\nA) case - This option doesn't make sense in the context of the sentence. The word \"case\" usually refers to a specific instance or situation, and it doesn't fit well here.\n\nB) reason - This option could work, as the boy could be saying that he doesn't know the reason for something. However, let's continue analyzing the other options to see if there's a better fit.\n\nC) how - This option doesn't make sense in the context of the sentence. The word \"how\" usually refers to the manner or way in which something is done, and it doesn't fit well here.\n\nD) because - This option seems to be the most appropriate choice. The boy is saying that he doesn't know why something happened, and it was just \"because.\" This word fits well in the context of the sentence and conveys the idea that the boy doesn't have a specific reason or explanation for something.\n\nE) answer - This option doesn't make sense in the context of the sentence. The word \"answer\" usually refers to a response or solution to a question or problem, and it doesn't fit well here.\n\nBased on the analysis of each option, the most appropriate word to complete the sentence is \"because.\" So the correct answer is:\n\nD) because",
