                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The question is asking what I may have extra of if I were to spit a lot without noticing. \n\nFirst, I need to understand what happens when I spit. When I spit, I am expelling saliva and any other substances in my mouth. \n\nNext, I need to consider the options given. \n\nOption A is phlegm, which is a thick mucus produced in the respiratory system. Since the question specifically mentions spitting, which is related to the mouth, it is unlikely that I would have extra phlegm. \n\nOption B is saliva and mouth, which is what I am already expelling when I spit. Therefore, this option does not make sense as an answer to the question. \n\nOption C is disease, which is a broad term that could refer to many different things. However, the question does not provide any context to suggest that I would have a disease from spitting. \n\nOption D is germs, which are microorganisms that can cause disease. While it is possible that I could have extra germs in my mouth if I were spitting a lot, the question specifically asks what I would have extra of, and germs are not a substance that I can physically accumulate. \n\nOption E is spittle, which is another word for saliva. Since spitting is related to expelling saliva, it makes sense that if I were to spit a lot without noticing, I would have extra spittle. \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is E) spittle.",
