                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Rephrased question: What might be the result of spitting a lot without realizing it?\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n\n- When we spit, we expel saliva and other fluids from our mouth.\n- If we do this a lot without noticing, it's possible that we may have an excess of something in our mouth or throat.\n- The options given are: phlegm, saliva and mouth, disease, germs, and spittle.\n- Phlegm is a thick, sticky substance that is produced by the respiratory system when we have an infection or inflammation. It is not directly related to spitting.\n- Saliva and mouth are not likely to be the \"extra\" thing we have, since they are already present in our mouth and spitting is a way to get rid of them.\n- Disease and germs are also not the most likely answers, since they are not directly related to spitting either.\n- Spittle, on the other hand, is a synonym for saliva and can be considered the \"extra\" thing we have if we are spitting a lot without realizing it.\n\nAnswer: E) spittle",
