                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "First, let's rephrase the question to ensure we understand it correctly: If I were to spit a lot without realizing it, what might I have an excess of?\n\nNow, let's work this out step by step by spelling out our thoughts and reasoning so anyone can verify them:\n\nA) Phlegm - Phlegm is a thick mucus produced in the respiratory system, and it is possible that an excess of phlegm could cause someone to spit more frequently.\n\nB) Saliva in the mouth - Saliva is a liquid produced by the salivary glands in the mouth, and having an excess of saliva could also lead to more frequent spitting.\n\nC) Disease - While certain diseases might cause an increase in saliva or phlegm production, the question is asking what you may have an excess of, not what might be causing the excess.\n\nD) Germs - Germs are microorganisms that can cause disease, but they are not directly related to the act of spitting.\n\nE) Spittle - Spittle is another term for saliva, so this option is similar to option B.\n\nBased on our analysis, the most appropriate answer is B) saliva in the mouth, as it directly relates to the act of spitting and is a substance that could be present in excess.",
