                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "To answer this question, we need to understand what each option means and how it relates to spitting a lot without noticing.\n\nA) Phlegm: Phlegm is a thick, sticky mucus produced by the respiratory system, usually in response to an infection or irritation. It is not typically associated with excessive spitting without noticing.\n\nB) Saliva and mouth: Saliva is a watery substance produced by the salivary glands in the mouth, which helps with digestion and keeps the mouth moist. Excessive saliva production could lead to increased spitting without noticing.\n\nC) Disease: A disease is a specific abnormal condition that negatively affects the structure or function of an organism. While some diseases may cause excessive spitting, it is not a direct cause of spitting without noticing.\n\nD) Germs: Germs are microscopic organisms, such as bacteria and viruses, that can cause disease. They are not directly related to spitting without noticing.\n\nE) Spittle: Spittle is another term for saliva or the frothy mixture of saliva and mucus that can be expelled from the mouth. This option is similar to option B.\n\nSub-questions:\n1) What causes excessive spitting without noticing?\n2) Which option is most closely related to excessive spitting without noticing?\n\nAnswers:\n1) Excessive spitting without noticing can be caused by increased saliva production, which may be due to various factors such as certain medications, medical conditions, or even spicy foods.\n2) Option B (saliva and mouth) and option E (spittle) are most closely related to excessive spitting without noticing, as they both involve saliva production.\n\nBased on the reasoning above, if you were to spit a lot without noticing, you may have extra saliva and mouth (option B) or spittle (option E).",
