                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nFirst, we need to understand what spitting is. Spitting is the act of forcefully expelling saliva or other substances from the mouth. \n\nIf someone is spitting a lot without noticing, it could be a sign of excessive saliva production or a habit of constantly spitting. \n\nIn this case, the answer would be B) saliva and mouth. The person may have extra saliva in their mouth that they are unconsciously spitting out. \n\nHowever, if the person is spitting due to an illness or infection, they may have extra phlegm, germs, or other symptoms associated with the disease. In that case, the answer would be A) phlegm, C) disease, or D) germs. \n\nBut without any additional information, the most likely answer is B) saliva and mouth.",
