                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Identify the situation - spitting a lot without noticing.\n\nStep 2: Determine what may be produced as a result - extra substance in the mouth.\n\nStep 3: Consider the options - phlegm, saliva, disease, germs, spittle.\n\nStep 4: Eliminate options that do not fit the situation - disease and germs are not produced by spitting.\n\nStep 5: Consider the remaining options - phlegm, saliva, spittle.\n\nStep 6: The most likely answer is saliva, as it is the most common substance produced in the mouth and can be increased by excessive spitting. Spittle is another word for saliva, so it is also a possible answer. Phlegm is less likely, as it is produced in the respiratory system and not directly related to spitting.\n\nTherefore, the answer is B) saliva and/or E) spittle.",
