                        "cot": " If you are spitting a lot, it means you are producing more saliva than usual. This could be due to a number of reasons, such as anxiety, dehydration, or even just eating spicy food. However, if you are producing more saliva than usual and you are not noticing it, it could mean that you have a medical condition called hypersalivation. Hypersalivation is when your body produces too much saliva, and it can be a symptom of a number of different conditions, such as GERD, diabetes, or even certain types of cancer. If you are producing more saliva than usual and you are not noticing it, you should see a doctor to find out the cause.",
