                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "To answer the question \"Who is the guard here for?\", we need to consider the context and purpose of the guard's presence. We can do this by examining each option and determining which one makes the most sense.\n\nA) Man post: A guard could be present to man a post, such as a security checkpoint or entrance to a restricted area. In this case, the guard would be there to ensure only authorized individuals are allowed access.\n\nB) Attack: A guard could be present to protect against potential attacks, such as in a military or high-security setting. In this case, the guard would be there to defend and respond to any threats.\n\nC) Intimidation: A guard could be present to intimidate or deter potential threats, such as in a high-crime area or during a high-profile event. In this case, the guard would be there to make their presence known and discourage any criminal activity.\n\nD) Prisoner: A guard could be present to watch over a prisoner, such as in a jail or detention facility. In this case, the guard would be there to ensure the prisoner does not escape and to maintain order within the facility.\n\nE) Unprotected: A guard could be present to protect an otherwise unprotected area or person, such as a VIP or a valuable asset. In this case, the guard would be there to provide security and prevent any harm or theft.\n\nWithout more context, it is impossible to definitively answer the original question. However, based on the options provided, we can conclude that the guard is present for one of the following reasons: to man a post, protect against attacks, intimidate potential threats, watch over a prisoner, or protect an unprotected area or person.",
