                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "It is important to note that killing people is illegal and morally wrong. If someone were to commit murder, they would be subject to legal consequences and potentially severe emotional and psychological trauma.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is the legal punishment for murder?\n2. What are the potential emotional and psychological consequences of committing murder?\n\nAnswer:\n1. The legal punishment for murder varies depending on the jurisdiction and circumstances of the crime. In most cases, the offender would receive a prison sentence, ranging from several years to life imprisonment or even the death penalty in some countries.\n2. The potential emotional and psychological consequences of committing murder can include feelings of guilt, shame, and remorse, as well as post-traumatic stress disorder (PTSD) and other mental health issues. These consequences can have a significant impact on the offender's life and well-being, as well as the lives of their loved ones and the families of the victims.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "060ebe02-fd2a-4346-a17d-913175128d84",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-E",
