                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Question Rephrase: If you were to begin taking the lives of others, what would you most likely experience as a result?\n\nStep 1: Analyze the options\nA) feelings of guilt - This is a possible emotional consequence of taking someone's life.\nB) prison sentence - This is a legal consequence of committing murder.\nC) terrible - This option is not clear or complete, so it can be eliminated.\nD) encouragement - It is unlikely that someone would receive encouragement for killing people.\nE) die - This option is not clear or complete, so it can be eliminated.\n\nStep 2: Determine the most likely consequence\nOut of the remaining options, the most likely consequence of killing people would be a prison sentence, as it is a legal consequence that society enforces to punish those who commit such acts.\n\nAnswer: B) prison sentence",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "c39a26da-6e65-44ad-be2b-c4b9936ac551",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-E",
