                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "To answer this question, we need to consider the consequences of killing people and how society and the individual would react to such actions. We can break this down into sub-questions:\n\n1. What are the emotional consequences of killing people?\n2. What are the legal consequences of killing people?\n3. How would society react to someone who kills people?\n\n1. Emotional consequences: Most people have a moral compass and empathy for others, which would likely lead to feelings of guilt and remorse after taking someone's life. So, option A) feelings of guilt is a likely consequence.\n\n2. Legal consequences: In most countries, killing someone is a serious crime, and the person responsible would likely face a prison sentence if caught and convicted. So, option B) prison sentence is a likely consequence.\n\n3. Societal reaction: Society generally condemns acts of violence, especially killing. It is unlikely that someone who kills people would receive encouragement from others. Instead, they would likely be ostracized and face negative consequences. Option D) encouragement is not a likely consequence.\n\nConsidering the above sub-questions, if you were to start killing people, you would be likely to receive:\n\nA) feelings of guilt\nB) prison sentence",
                        "answers": [
