                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nThe correct answer is A) cloud.\n\nSnowflakes form when water vapor in the atmosphere condenses into tiny ice crystals. These ice crystals form in clouds when the temperature is below freezing. As the ice crystals fall through the atmosphere, they collect more water vapor and grow into snowflakes. The snowflakes then fall to the ground when the temperature is below freezing. Therefore, the answer is A) cloud, as this is where the snowflakes form.",
