                    {
                        "id": "8ea6e271-b907-459d-9b39-0fe2a4d3c59b",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-16",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "To answer this question, we need to consider the risk factors and characteristics of each type of melanoma and determine which one is most likely for this patient based on her age, ethnicity, family history, and lifestyle.\n\nA) Desmoplastic melanoma is a rare type of melanoma that typically occurs in older individuals and is more common in sun-damaged skin. It is not specifically associated with African-American individuals.\n\nB) Nodular melanoma is an aggressive form of melanoma that can occur in any age group and is not specifically associated with African-American individuals.\n\nC) Acral lentiginous melanoma is more common in people with darker skin, such as African-Americans and Asians. It typically occurs on the palms, soles, and under the nails.\n\nD) Lentigo maligna melanoma is a slow-growing type of melanoma that typically occurs in older individuals with a history of sun exposure. It is not specifically associated with African-American individuals.\n\nE) Superficial spreading melanoma is the most common type of melanoma and can occur in any age group. It is not specifically associated with African-American individuals.\n\nSub-questions:\n1) Which type of melanoma is more common in African-American individuals?\nAnswer: Acral lentiginous melanoma.\n\n2) Which type of melanoma is associated with sun exposure?\nAnswer: Lentigo maligna melanoma.\n\nConsidering the patient's age, ethnicity, family history, and lifestyle, she is at the greatest risk of developing acral lentiginous melanoma (C). This type of melanoma is more common in African-American individuals and is not specifically associated with sun exposure, which is relevant given her regular travels to the Caribbean.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "9bbcef06-0f63-4232-98aa-da9d4a8d6958",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-E",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "C) Acral lentiginous melanoma.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "C",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
                        ],
                        "author": "thoughtsource",
                        "date": "2023/04/12 20:27:42",
                        "api_service": "openai_chat",
