                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nStep 1: Understand the patient's risk factors. The patient is an African-American woman, 44 years old, with no history of serious illness and no medication use. She has been working in a law firm for the past 20 years and travels to the Caribbean regularly with her husband.\n\nStep 2: Understand the types of melanoma. Desmoplastic melanoma is a rare type of melanoma that is usually found in older adults and is more common in men than women. Nodular melanoma is the most common type of melanoma and is usually found in adults. Acral lentiginous melanoma is the most common type of melanoma in African-Americans and is usually found on the palms, soles, and under the nails. Lentigo maligna melanoma is a type of melanoma that is usually found in older adults and is more common in women than men. Superficial spreading melanoma is the most common type of melanoma and is usually found in adults.\n\nStep 3: Compare the patient's risk factors to the types of melanoma. The patient is an African-American woman, 44 years old, with no history of serious illness and no medication use. She has been working in a law firm for the past 20 years and travels to the Caribbean regularly with her husband. Based on these risk factors, the patient is at greatest risk of acral lentiginous melanoma, which is the most common type of melanoma in African-Americans and is usually found on the palms, soles, and under the nails.\n\nAnswer: C) Acral lentiginous",
