                        "cot_trigger": "lievin-02",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Let's use step by step inductive reasoning, given the medical nature of the question. \n\nThe first thing to note is that the ultrasound shows an intrauterine heteroechoic mass. This means that there is a mass inside the uterus that is not of uniform density. This could be caused by a number of things, but the most likely cause is a tumor.\n\nThe next thing to note is that the ovaries are enlarged and have multiple thin-walled, septated cysts with clear content. This is most likely caused by a condition called polycystic ovarian syndrome (PCOS).\n\n PCOS is a condition that affects the ovaries and is characterized by the presence of multiple small cysts on the ovaries. The cysts are usually filled with clear fluid. PCOS is a common cause of enlarged ovaries and is often associated with other symptoms such as irregular periods, excess hair growth, and weight gain.\n\nThe most likely cause of the ovarian findings is polycystic ovarian syndrome (PCOS).",
