                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Plan:\n1. Identify the characteristics of the intrauterine mass and rule out any identifiable fetus or amniotic fluid.\n2. Focus on the ovarian findings and identify the type of cysts present.\n3. Match the characteristics of the cysts with the options given to determine the most likely cause.\n\nAnswer: E) Theca lutein cysts\n\nExplanation:\n1. The intrauterine mass with numerous anechoic spaces and no identifiable fetus or amniotic fluid is consistent with a molar pregnancy.\n2. The enlarged ovaries with multiple thin-walled, septated cysts with clear content are consistent with theca lutein cysts.\n3. Theca lutein cysts are associated with molar pregnancies and are caused by excessive stimulation of the ovaries by human chorionic gonadotropin (hCG) produced by the molar pregnancy. Therefore, the most likely cause of the ovarian findings in this case is theca lutein cysts.",
