                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The presence of an intrauterine heteroechoic mass with numerous anechoic spaces and no identifiable fetus or amniotic fluid suggests a molar pregnancy or a hydatidiform mole. This is a type of gestational trophoblastic disease that arises from abnormal fertilization of an egg without a nucleus or an egg that is fertilized by two sperm. The cystic structures in the ovaries are likely related to the molar pregnancy and are called theca lutein cysts. These cysts are caused by high levels of human chorionic gonadotropin (hCG) produced by the abnormal placenta in a molar pregnancy. Therefore, the correct answer is E) Theca lutein cysts.",
