                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "C) Conversion of aminolevulinic acid to porphobilinogen. This process is involved in heme synthesis, and impairment of this process could lead to sideroblastic anemia, which is characterized by basophilic stippling. Although sideroblastic anemia does not typically cause the developmental delays seen in this patient, it is the most likely impaired process among the given options, as it best explains the anemia and basophilic stippling observed in the patient.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "C",
