                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Plan:\n1. Understand the patient's condition and the characteristics of the tumor.\n2. Review the common metastatic sites for this type of tumor.\n3. Analyze the options and choose the most likely initial metastatic site based on the information provided.\n\nAnswer:\nThe patient has a thyroid nodule that is suspicious for neoplasia. The planned treatment is radioiodine therapy after near-total thyroidectomy. The question asks for the most likely initial metastatic site in this patient.\n\nAccording to the American Thyroid Association, the most common sites of distant metastases for differentiated thyroid cancer (DTC) are the lungs and bones. However, in this case, the CT scan was performed to check for any lesions in these sites, indicating that they are not the initial metastatic site.\n\nThe tumor is located in the thyroid gland, and the most likely initial metastatic site would be the cervical lymph nodes. The lymphatic drainage of the thyroid gland is primarily to the cervical lymph nodes, and metastases to these nodes are common in thyroid cancer.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C) Cervical lymph nodes.",
