                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Let's think step by step about how we can answer this question. \n\nFirst, we need to understand what the LOD score is. The LOD score is a measure of how likely it is that two loci are linked. The higher the LOD score, the more likely it is that the loci are linked. \n\nNow that we know what the LOD score is, we can look at the answer choices and see which one is most likely to be correct. \n\nChoice A says that the LOD score is less than 1. This means that it is very unlikely that the two loci are linked. \n\nChoice B says that the LOD score is less than 2. This means that it is somewhat unlikely that the two loci are linked. \n\nChoice C says that the LOD score is greater than 3. This means that it is very likely that the two loci are linked. \n\nChoice D says that the LOD score is equal to 0. This means that it is impossible to say whether or not the two loci are linked. \n\nBased on this information, the best answer is C.",
