                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The LOD score is a statistical measure used to determine the likelihood of two loci being linked on a chromosome. A LOD score of 3 or higher is generally considered significant evidence for linkage, while a LOD score of less than 3 suggests that the evidence for linkage is weaker.\n\nTherefore, the answer is B) LOD Score < 3. If the novel mutation in the CFTR gene is found to be closely linked to the \u0394F508 mutation, we would expect to see a LOD score of 3 or higher. A LOD score of less than 3 would suggest that the two loci are not as closely linked, and therefore less likely to be inherited together.",
