                    {
                        "id": "5eb5bebc-9534-4350-bbf9-911aa93efdf5",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-13",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nFirst, let's rephrase the question to be sure we understood it correctly. \n\nWe are trying to find out which of the following would most likely suggest that two loci have a high probability of being closely linked. \n\nA) LOD Score < 1\nB) LOD Score < 3\nC) LOD Score < 2\nD) LOD Score > 3\nE) LOD Score = 0\n\nSecond, let's work this out step by step by spelling out our thoughts & reasoning so anyone can verify them.\n\nThe LOD score is a measure of how likely it is that two loci are linked. A LOD score of < 1 means that it is very unlikely that the two loci are linked, while a LOD score of > 3 means that it is very likely that the two loci are linked. Therefore, the answer must be either B) LOD Score < 3 or C) LOD Score < 2. \n\nThird, make sure we have the right answer.\n\nThe correct answer is C) LOD Score < 2.",
