                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nStudent: What does LOD stand for?\n\nProfessor: LOD stands for logarithm of the odds. It's a statistical measure used to determine whether two loci are linked.\n\nStudent: What's the difference between a LOD score of 1 and a LOD score of 3?\n\nProfessor: A LOD score of 1 means that there's a 1 in 10,000 chance that the two loci are linked. A LOD score of 3 means that there's a 1 in 1,000,000 chance that the two loci are linked. So a LOD score of 3 is much more significant than a LOD score of 1.",
