                        "instruction": "qa-10",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nStep 1: Understand the question. Researchers are studying the inheritance pattern of mutations in the CFTR gene, and they believe that there is a novel mutation in the population they are studying. The question is asking which of the following would most likely suggest that these two loci have a high probability of being closely linked.\n\nStep 2: Understand the answer choices. The answer choices are A) LOD Score < 1, B) LOD Score < 3, C) LOD Score < 2, D) LOD Score > 3, and E) LOD Score = 0.\n\nStep 3: Understand the concept of a LOD Score. A LOD Score (logarithm of the odds score) is a measure of the strength of the evidence for linkage between two loci. A LOD Score of 3 or higher is considered to be strong evidence for linkage, while a LOD Score of 1 or lower is considered to be weak evidence for linkage.\n\nStep 4: Choose the correct answer. The correct answer is D) LOD Score > 3, as this would suggest that the two loci have a high probability of being closely linked.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "a983f431-e4a7-4156-829c-dd7eeda78956",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-E",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": " D) LOD Score > 3.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "D",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
                        ],
                        "author": "thoughtsource",
                        "date": "2023/04/17 14:11:44",
                        "api_service": "openai",
                        "model": "{'name': 'text-davinci-003', 'temperature': 0, 'max_tokens': 512}",
