                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nThe correct answer is C) LOD Score < 2.\n\nLOD stands for logarithm of the odds, and is a measure of the likelihood that two loci (in this case, the \u0394F508 mutation and the novel mutation) are linked. A LOD Score of less than 2 indicates that the two loci are likely to be closely linked, while a LOD Score of greater than 3 indicates that the two loci are likely to be unlinked. A LOD Score of 0 indicates that the two loci are equally likely to be linked or unlinked. Therefore, C) LOD Score < 2 is the correct answer.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "56b8c6aa-eb16-4832-9b62-7047dc9ee2da",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-E",
