                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nThe next best step in the management of this patient is to order an ACTH stimulation test. This test is used to diagnose adrenal insufficiency, which is a possible cause of the patient's symptoms. The test involves measuring the patient's cortisol levels before and after administering a synthetic form of the hormone ACTH. If the cortisol levels do not increase after the administration of ACTH, it is likely that the patient has adrenal insufficiency. If the test is positive, then the patient should be started on hydrocortisone and fludrocortisone therapy. Androgen replacement treatment is not indicated in this case.",
