                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nStep 1: Rephrase the question: What is the next best step in the management of a 30-year-old man with excessive fatigue, weakness, abdominal pain, constipation, and weight loss over the last 2 weeks, who has a bronze discoloration to his skin?\n\nStep 2: Analyze the patient's symptoms: The patient's symptoms suggest a possible endocrine disorder, such as Addison's disease. The bronze discoloration to his skin is a classic sign of Addison's disease.\n\nStep 3: Consider the best course of action: The best course of action would be to order an ACTH stimulation test to confirm the diagnosis of Addison's disease. This test measures the body's response to a synthetic form of the hormone adrenocorticotropic hormone (ACTH). If the test results are positive, then the patient can be started on both hydrocortisone and fludrocortisone therapy.\n\nAnswer: E) Order an ACTH stimulation test",
