                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nF) Order a serum cortisol level\n\nThe next best step in the management of this patient is to order a serum cortisol level. This is because the patient's symptoms and physical examination findings are suggestive of adrenal insufficiency, which is a condition in which the adrenal glands do not produce enough cortisol. A serum cortisol level can be used to diagnose adrenal insufficiency and determine the severity of the condition. If the serum cortisol level is low, then further testing, such as an ACTH stimulation test, may be necessary to confirm the diagnosis. Depending on the results of the serum cortisol level, the physician may then decide to start the patient on hydrocortisone and/or fludrocortisone therapy.",
