                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": " D. PCR is the most sensitive and specific test for detecting HIV infection, and is the preferred method for diagnosing HIV in infants. It is used to detect the genetic material of HIV in the baby's blood, and can detect the virus even if the mother has been taking her medications.",
