                    },
                    {
                        "id": "46bd7884-861f-4fc8-9be8-489e80d9e381",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-16",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nThe first step is to understand the context of the question. HIV is a virus that is transmitted through bodily fluids, and can be passed from mother to child during pregnancy, childbirth, or breastfeeding. The mother in this case is HIV positive, and the obstetrician is worried that the child may have been infected due to the mother's haphazard use of her anti-retroviral medications.\n\nTo answer the question, it is important to understand the different types of assays that can be used to detect the genetic material of HIV. \n\nEnzyme-linked immunosorbent assay (ELISA) is a type of antibody test that detects the presence of antibodies to HIV in the blood. It is a relatively quick and inexpensive test, but it is not very accurate and can produce false positive results.\n\nWestern blot is a more accurate test than ELISA, and is used to confirm a positive ELISA result. It detects the presence of specific proteins in the blood that are associated with HIV infection.\n\nRapid HIV antibody test is a type of ELISA test that can provide results in as little as 20 minutes. It is used to detect the presence of antibodies to HIV in the blood.\n\nPolymerase chain reaction (PCR) is a type of test that can detect the genetic material of HIV in the blood. It is a very sensitive and accurate test, but it is also expensive and time-consuming.\n\nSouthern blot is a type of test that can detect the presence of HIV genetic material in the blood. It is a very sensitive and accurate test, but it is also expensive and time-consuming.\n\nBased on this information, the correct answer is D) Polymerase chain reaction (PCR).",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "af45975b-7940-472f-8fe3-8086a036472e",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-E",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": " D) Polymerase chain reaction (PCR).",
                                "answer_from_choices": "D",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
                        ],
                        "author": "thoughtsource",
                        "date": "2023/04/17 14:13:39",
                        "api_service": "openai",
                        "model": "{'name': 'text-davinci-003', 'temperature': 0, 'max_tokens': 512}",
