                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "D) Polymerase chain reaction\n\nCritique: ELISA, Western blot, and rapid HIV antibody tests are used to detect antibodies produced by the body in response to HIV infection, but they may not be reliable in detecting HIV in infants born to HIV-positive mothers due to the presence of maternal antibodies. Southern blot is a technique used to detect specific DNA sequences, but it is not commonly used for HIV diagnosis. Polymerase chain reaction (PCR) is a highly sensitive and specific test that can detect the genetic material (RNA) of HIV in the blood of infected individuals, including infants born to HIV-positive mothers.\n\nFinal answer: D) Polymerase chain reaction.",
