                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Let's differentiate using step by step reasoning like a medical expert. \n\nSystemic vascular resistance is the resistance to blood flow throughout the body. This would not be decreased in response to the patient's current condition. \n\nFractional tissue oxygen extraction is the amount of oxygen that is extracted from the blood by the tissues. This would not be decreased in response to the patient's current condition. \n\nCarotid baroreceptor firing activity is the activity of the baroreceptors in the carotid arteries. This would not be decreased in response to the patient's current condition. \n\nCardiac inotropy is the contractility of the heart. This would be decreased in response to the patient's current condition.",
