ardiac inotropy is decreased.\n\nBased on the information provided, the most likely answer is A) Systemic vascular resistance. The patient's low blood pressure, decreased radial pulses, and pale appearance suggest that systemic vascular resistance is decreased compared to a healthy adult.",
