                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nThe patient has a non-tender spine with normal mobility in all 4 directions. This suggests that he does not have a compression fracture.\nA) Compression fracture\n\nThe patient has a past medical history of osteoporosis, dyslipidemia, and diabetes. These conditions can cause weakening of the bones and make them more prone to fractures.\nB) Herniated nucleus pulposus\n\nThe patient has a non-tender spine with normal mobility in all 4 directions. This suggests that he does not have a herniated nucleus pulposus.\nC) Musculoskeletal strain\n\nThe patient has a non-tender spine with normal mobility in all 4 directions. This suggests that he does not have a musculoskeletal strain.\nD) Spinal stenosis\n\nThe patient has a non-tender spine with normal mobility in all 4 directions. This suggests that he does not have spinal stenosis.\nE) Vascular claudication\n\nThe patient has a non-tender spine with normal mobility in all 4 directions. This suggests that he does not have vascular claudication.",
