                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nThe most likely diagnosis in this case is C) Musculoskeletal strain. \n\nThis is based on the patient's history of gradually worsening back pain that worsened after moving furniture, as well as the fact that the patient experiences relief when riding his bike or pushing a cart at the grocery store. This suggests that the pain is due to a musculoskeletal strain, which is an injury to the muscles, tendons, or ligaments caused by overstretching or overuse. \n\nThe physical exam findings of a non-tender spine with normal mobility in all 4 directions also support the diagnosis of musculoskeletal strain. Compression fractures, herniated nucleus pulposus, spinal stenosis, and vascular claudication are all unlikely in this case, as they would likely cause more severe pain and tenderness on physical exam. \n\nRadiography of the spine and basic labs may be helpful in confirming the diagnosis, as they can help rule out other potential causes of the patient's back pain.",
