                                "id": "bca3ee53-b07c-4867-be75-810b0629ffe1",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-E",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "E) Carotid artery dissection. However, it is important to note that this is less likely than DVT as the cause of the patient's symptoms. Carotid artery dissection is a tear in the lining of the carotid artery, which can cause a stroke. However, this is less likely in this case because the patient's symptoms are more consistent with a DVT. Further evaluation, such as a Doppler ultrasound or CT scan, would be needed to confirm the diagnosis of DVT and rule out other possible causes.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "E",
