                        "instruction": "zhou-01-ins",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Identify the main problem and relevant information\nThe main problem is sudden weakness of the right arm and leg. Relevant information includes the patient's age, recent travel history, smoking history, medication history, vital signs, and physical examination findings.\n\nStep 2: Formulate a differential diagnosis\nBased on the information provided, possible causes of the patient's symptoms include stroke, deep vein thrombosis (DVT), pulmonary embolism (PE), and cardiac sources of emboli such as patent foramen ovale, atrial myxoma, mitral valve vegetation, and atrial fibrillation. Carotid artery dissection is also a possibility.\n\nStep 3: Determine the most likely diagnosis\nGiven the patient's symptoms, physical examination findings, and risk factors, the most likely diagnosis is a stroke. The presence of a swollen, erythematous, and tender left lower leg suggests the possibility of DVT or PE, but these conditions alone would not explain the patient's neurological symptoms.\n\nStep 4: Order appropriate diagnostic tests\nTo confirm the diagnosis of stroke and rule out other possible causes, the following tests may be ordered:\n- CT scan or MRI of the brain to assess for ischemic or hemorrhagic stroke\n- Doppler ultrasound or CT angiography of the lower extremities to assess for DVT or PE\n- Echocardiogram to assess for cardiac sources of emboli\n\nStep 5: Develop a treatment plan\nIf the diagnosis of stroke is confirmed, the patient may be treated with thrombolytic therapy or mechanical thrombectomy if eligible. Blood pressure control and anticoagulation may also be initiated to prevent further strokes. If DVT or PE is diagnosed, anticoagulation therapy will be initiated. If a cardiac source of emboli is identified, appropriate management will be initiated based on the underlying condition. Smoking cessation counseling may also be provided.",
