                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nFirst, let's rephrase the question to make sure we understand it correctly: What further evaluation is most likely to show in a 35-year-old woman who has sudden weakness of her right arm and leg that started 3 hours ago, has smoked a pack of cigarettes daily for 10 years, and has a temperature of 38.0\u00b0C (100.4\u00b0F), pulse of 115/min and regular, and blood pressure of 155/85 mm Hg?\n\nSecond, let's work this out step by step by spelling out our thoughts & reasoning so anyone can verify them: \nGiven the patient's symptoms and history, the most likely diagnosis is a deep vein thrombosis (DVT). This is a condition in which a blood clot forms in a deep vein, usually in the leg, and can cause swelling, pain, and decreased muscle strength. The presence of a Babinski sign on the right side is also suggestive of a DVT.\n\nThird, make sure we have the right answer: The correct answer is E) Carotid artery dissection.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "49a0e929-0c04-43fb-9906-52c700f6bd5b",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-E",
