                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Let's derive the differential diagnosis step by step: \n\nThe patient has a severe cough and difficulty breathing. He also has a cough that appears only at night, which is persistent enough to wake him up from sleep.\n\nThe differential diagnosis for a severe cough and difficulty breathing includes:\n\n-Asthma\n-Bronchitis\n-Chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD)\n-Pneumonia\n\nThe differential diagnosis for a cough that appears only at night and is persistent enough to wake the patient up from sleep includes:\n\n-Asthma\n-Gastroesophageal reflux disease (GERD)\n-Postnasal drip\n\nThe patient also mentions that he has had a 'heart attack' 5 years ago. He has brought his lab reports which he had recently got done on the suggestions of his family doctor. An electrocardiogram (ECG) and a chest X-ray are found.\n\nThe differential diagnosis for a patient with a history of a 'heart attack' and an abnormal ECG and chest X-ray includes:\n\n-Aortic stenosis\n-Mitral stenosis\n-Pulmonary embolism\n\nThe next step in this patient's management is a computed tomography (CT) scan.",
