                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Let's differentiate using step by step reasoning like a medical expert. \n\nThe first thing to consider is the patient's age. 55 years old is the age when heart disease becomes more common. The patient's symptoms of severe coughing and difficulty breathing are also indicative of heart disease. The patient's history of a heart attack 5 years ago and his continued alcohol consumption despite his doctor's advice are also risk factors for heart disease.\n\nThe next step in this patient's management would be to order an echocardiogram. This will help to assess the function of the patient's heart and to look for any structural abnormalities.",
