                        "cot_trigger": "kojima-01",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Let's think step by step. The first thing this patient needs is a thorough history and physical examination. This will help to rule out other potential causes of his symptoms, such as a pulmonary embolism. Once that has been ruled out, the next step would be to order an electrocardiogram (ECG) and a chest X-ray. These will help to determine if the patient is experiencing a heart attack or if there is any other cardiac abnormality. If the ECG and chest X-ray are normal, the next step would be to order a stress test. This will help to determine if the patient's symptoms are due to coronary artery disease. If the stress test is positive, the next step would be to order a cardiac catheterization.",
