                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The correct answer is D) Stress test.\nThis patient is likely to have a condition called cor pulmonale, which is characterized by right ventricular failure due to pulmonary hypertension. This can be caused by a number of conditions, including COPD, pulmonary embolism, or cor pulmonale. The chest X-ray shows signs of right ventricular enlargement, and the ECG shows right ventricular strain. A stress test would be the next step in this patient's management, to determine the cause of the pulmonary hypertension.",
