                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The patient is presenting with symptoms of shortness of breath, cough, and difficulty breathing, which are suggestive of a respiratory or cardiac issue. He also has a history of a heart attack and continues to consume alcohol despite medical advice. The ECG and chest X-ray may provide some clues to the underlying cause of his symptoms. \n\nThe next step in this patient's management would be to perform a C) Echocardiogram. This test will help evaluate the structure and function of the heart, including the size of the chambers, the thickness of the heart muscle, and the function of the heart valves. It can also help identify any abnormalities in the heart's pumping ability, which may be contributing to the patient's symptoms. \n\nAngiography may be considered if there is suspicion of a blockage in the coronary arteries, but this would not be the first-line investigation in this case. A stress test may also be considered to evaluate the heart's response to exercise, but an echocardiogram would be a more appropriate initial investigation. Cardiac biopsy would not be indicated at this stage.",
                        "answers": [
