                        "cot": "\nFirst, it is important to note that the patient has a history of a heart attack and is continuing to consume alcohol despite his doctor's advice.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is the patient's current condition?\n2. What is the purpose of the lab reports?\n\nThe patient is presenting with a severe cough and difficulty breathing, which worsens at night. The lab reports were done on the suggestion of the family doctor. The ECG and chest X-ray have been done.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What do the ECG and chest X-ray results indicate?\n2. What further tests are needed to diagnose the patient's condition?\n\nThe ECG and chest X-ray results indicate that the patient may have a cardiac condition. Further tests such as an echocardiogram, stress test, and angiography may be needed to diagnose the patient's condition.\n\nAnswer: C) Echocardiogram",
