                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nProfessor: Alright, so the patient has a severe cough and difficulty breathing, and has had a heart attack 5 years ago. He has also brought his lab reports, and an ECG and chest X-ray have been done. So, what do you think is the next step in this patient's management?\n\nStudent: I think it's either an angiography, a computed tomography (CT), an echocardiogram, a stress test, or a cardiac biopsy.\n\nProfessor: That's right. Now, let's think about which of these tests would be most appropriate for this patient. An angiography is a test that looks at the blood vessels in the heart, so it would be useful if we were looking for blockages in the coronary arteries. A CT scan is a type of imaging test that looks at the structure of the heart, so it would be useful if we were looking for any structural abnormalities. An echocardiogram is an ultrasound test that looks at the function of the heart, so it would be useful if we were looking for any functional abnormalities. A stress test is a test that looks at how the heart responds to physical activity, so it would be useful if we were looking for any signs of heart disease. And finally, a cardiac biopsy is a test that looks at the tissue of the heart, so it would be useful if we were looking for any signs of inflammation or infection.\n\nStudent: So, based on the patient's symptoms and lab results, the most appropriate test would be an echocardiogram.\n\nProfessor: That's correct. An echocardiogram would be the most appropriate test for this patient, as it would allow us to assess the function of the heart and look for any functional abnormalities.",
