                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: The thymus is an important organ in the immune system, responsible for the development and maturation of T cells. Germinal centers are areas within lymph nodes where B cells undergo proliferation and differentiation in response to an antigen. Defects in genes involved in immune system function can lead to immunodeficiency disorders.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is the significance of an absent thymic shadow?\n2. What is the significance of the absence of germinal centers in a lymph node biopsy?\n3. What are the functions of the genes listed in the answer choices?\n4. Which of these genes is most commonly associated with the symptoms described in the patient?\n\nAnswers:\n1. An absent thymic shadow indicates that the thymus is not visible on a chest X-ray, which can be a sign of thymic hypoplasia or aplasia.\n2. The absence of germinal centers in a lymph node biopsy suggests a defect in B cell function, as these centers are where B cells undergo proliferation and differentiation in response to an antigen.\n3. WASP (Wiskott-Aldrich syndrome protein) is involved in cytoskeletal organization and signaling in immune cells. ATM (ataxia-telangiectasia mutated) is involved in DNA repair and cell cycle control. Adenosine deaminase is an enzyme involved in purine metabolism and lymphocyte development. NADPH oxidase is involved in the production of reactive oxygen species by phagocytes. BTK (Bruton's tyrosine kinase) is involved in B cell development and signaling.\n4. The symptoms described in the patient are consistent with a combined immunodeficiency disorder, which is most commonly associated with defects in the WASP gene. Therefore, the most likely cause of this patient's symptoms is A) Defect in WASP gene.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "e470ba3e-25fd-41c8-8d7c-c8a6dae40362",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-E",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "A) Defect in WASP gene.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "A",
                                "correct_answer": false
                            }
                        ],
