cause X-linked agammaglobulinemia, which is characterized by a lack of B cells and low immunoglobulin levels, leading to recurrent infections. Does this match our patient's symptoms?\n\nStudent: No, it doesn't.\n\nProfessor: So, based on our analysis, which answer choice is the most likely cause of this patient's symptoms?\n\nStudent: The",
