                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nFirst, it is important to note that the patient is a 2-month-old girl and has had multiple bacterial and viral infections, chronic diarrhea, and has failed to gain weight since her uncomplicated delivery.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What are the common causes of failure to gain weight in infants?\n2. What are the common causes of chronic diarrhea in infants?\n3. What are the common causes of multiple bacterial and viral infections in infants?\n\nAnswer to sub-question 1: Common causes of failure to gain weight in infants include inadequate caloric intake, malabsorption, and metabolic disorders.\n\nAnswer to sub-question 2: Common causes of chronic diarrhea in infants include infections, food allergies, and malabsorption.\n\nAnswer to sub-question 3: Common causes of multiple bacterial and viral infections in infants include immunodeficiencies.\n\nGiven the patient's symptoms and the absent thymic shadow noted during the workup, as well as the lymph node biopsy demonstrating the absence of germinal centers, the most likely cause of the patient's symptoms is adenosine deaminase deficiency (C). Adenosine deaminase deficiency is an immunodeficiency disorder that can cause failure to gain weight, chronic diarrhea, and multiple bacterial and viral infections.",
