                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nProfessor: Alright, so the patient has failed to gain weight, has had chronic diarrhea, and has had multiple bacterial and viral infections. We can rule out A and E because they are related to WASP and BTK genes, which are not related to the patient's symptoms. \n\nStudent: So, that leaves us with C, Adenosine deaminase deficiency, and D, NADPH oxidase deficiency. How do we decide between the two?\n\nProfessor: Well, Adenosine deaminase deficiency is a genetic disorder that affects the immune system, which is consistent with the patient's multiple bacterial and viral infections. NADPH oxidase deficiency, on the other hand, is a disorder that affects the production of reactive oxygen species, which is not related to the patient's symptoms. Therefore, the most likely cause of the patient's symptoms is Adenosine deaminase deficiency.",
