            {
                "id": "med_qa_test_676",
                "ref_id": "",
                "question": "A 75-year-old man is admitted to the hospital because of a 3-day history of a productive cough and shortness of breath. His temperature is 38\u00b0C (100.4\u00b0F) and respirations are 32/min. Crackles are heard over the right upper and the entire left lung fields. Sputum culture confirms infection with Streptococcus pneumoniae. Despite appropriate therapy, the patient dies. A photomicrograph of a section of the lung obtained during the autopsy is shown. Which of the following mediators is most likely responsible for the presence of the cell-type indicated by the arrow?",
                "type": "multiplechoice",
                "choices": [
                    "Immunoglobulin E",
                    "Platelet activating factor",
                    "Interferon-gamma",
                    "Interleukin-10",
                    "Leukotriene D4"
