                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nStep 1: Understand the question. The question is asking which of the five mediators is most likely responsible for the presence of the cell-type indicated by the arrow in the photomicrograph of a section of the lung obtained during the autopsy.\n\nStep 2: Research the mediators. Research each of the five mediators to understand their roles in the body.\n\nStep 3: Analyze the photomicrograph. Examine the photomicrograph to determine the type of cell indicated by the arrow.\n\nStep 4: Compare the mediators to the cell type. Compare the roles of the five mediators to the type of cell indicated by the arrow in the photomicrograph.\n\nStep 5: Answer the question. Based on the research and analysis, the most likely mediator responsible for the presence of the cell-type indicated by the arrow is Interferon-gamma (C).",
