                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nAnswer: B) Platelet activating factor\n\nExplanation: The photomicrograph shows an accumulation of neutrophils, which are a type of white blood cell that is released in response to infection. Platelet activating factor is a mediator that is released in response to infection and is responsible for the recruitment of neutrophils to the site of infection. Therefore, Platelet activating factor is the most likely mediator responsible for the presence of the cell-type indicated by the arrow.",
