 such as methicillin-resistant Staphylococcus aureus (MRSA).\n\nStudent: And IV fluids and monitoring would be for a less severe case or a different diagnosis altogether?\n\nProfessor: IV fluids and monitoring would be appropriate for a patient with a less severe presentation or a different diagnosis, such as viral gastroenteritis or dehydration.\n\nStudent: Based on the patient's symptoms and CSF results,",
