                        "instruction": "qa-13",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nFirst, let's rephrase the question to make sure we understand it correctly: What acid-base disturbance is most likely associated with a 1-month-old girl who is brought to the emergency department with persistent vomiting, dehydration, and irritability?\n\nSecond, let's work this out step by step by spelling out our thoughts & reasoning so anyone can verify them:\n\nThe patient is exhibiting signs of dehydration, which can lead to an electrolyte imbalance. Electrolyte imbalances can cause acid-base disturbances. The patient's vital signs indicate a low blood pressure (85/55 mm Hg) and a high heart rate (150/min). These signs are consistent with a metabolic acidosis, which is an acid-base disturbance caused by an accumulation of acids in the body.\n\nThird, make sure we have the right answer:\n\nThe acid-base disturbance most likely associated with this patient's condition is a metabolic acidosis (Answer C).",
