                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nAnswer: D) Type II pneumocytes\n\nExplanation: Betamethasone is a corticosteroid medication that is used to treat preterm labor. It works by stimulating the production of type II pneumocytes, which are specialized cells in the fetal lungs that produce surfactant. Surfactant is a substance that helps keep the air sacs in the lungs open, allowing the baby to breathe more easily. By stimulating the production of type II pneumocytes, betamethasone helps to reduce the risk of preterm labor and improve the baby's chances of survival.",
