                        "cot": "\nAnswer: D) Type II pneumocytes\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n\n1. Betamethasone is a steroid medication used to treat preterm labor.\n2. Steroid medications are known to stimulate the production of surfactant in the lungs of the fetus.\n3. Surfactant is a mixture of lipids and proteins produced by type II pneumocytes in the lungs of the fetus.\n4. Therefore, betamethasone stimulates type II pneumocytes in the lungs of the fetus.",
