                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The patient is a 66-year-old man with a cough, fatigue, confusion, diabetes, and hypertension. His vital signs show a fever, low blood pressure, tachycardia, and crackles on pulmonary exam and S4 on cardiac auscultation. These findings suggest a possible pneumonia and/or sepsis. The next best step in management would be to administer antibiotics and admit the patient to the hospital. Option A and B are not appropriate as the patient needs antibiotics and admission to the hospital. Option C is not necessary as the patient does not require admission to the intensive care unit at this time. Option E is not the best choice as it only includes one antibiotic and the patient may need broader coverage. Therefore, the best option is D, which includes two antibiotics and admission to the intensive care unit for close monitoring.",
