                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nAnswer: D) Ceftriaxone, azithromycin, and admission to the intensive care unit.\n\nThe patient's symptoms and physical exam findings suggest a possible infection, so the next best step in management is to start antibiotics. Ceftriaxone and azithromycin are broad-spectrum antibiotics that can cover a variety of bacterial infections. Additionally, the patient's age and underlying medical conditions put him at higher risk for complications, so admission to the intensive care unit is recommended for close monitoring.",
