                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nThe next best step in management is D) Ceftriaxone, azithromycin, and admission to the intensive care unit. \n\nThe patient's temperature is elevated, which could indicate an infection. The physical exam reveals crackles on pulmonary exam and S4 on cardiac auscultation, which could indicate pneumonia or congestive heart failure. Therefore, it is important to treat the patient with antibiotics to address the potential infection. Ceftriaxone is a broad-spectrum antibiotic that is effective against a wide range of bacteria, including those that cause pneumonia. Azithromycin is a macrolide antibiotic that is effective against atypical bacteria, which can cause pneumonia. \n\nGiven the patient's age and the severity of his symptoms, it is important to admit him to the intensive care unit for further monitoring and treatment. The intensive care unit is better equipped to handle the patient's needs and provide the necessary care.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "160f0e06-81a3-479d-9d82-8666603daf36",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-E",
