                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nFirst, it is important to note that the patient is elderly and has multiple chronic conditions. Additionally, the patient has a fever and crackles on pulmonary exam, as well as an S4 on cardiac auscultation.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is the most likely cause of the patient's symptoms?\n2. What is the best course of treatment for this condition?\n3. Is admission to the hospital necessary?\n\nAnswer:\n1. The patient's symptoms are most likely due to a respiratory infection.\n2. The best course of treatment is likely to be a combination of antibiotics, such as ceftriaxone and azithromycin.\n3. Given the patient's age and chronic conditions, admission to the hospital is necessary.\n\nTherefore, the next best step in management is D) Ceftriaxone, azithromycin, and admission to the intensive care unit.",
