                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Rephrased question: Based on the patient's lab values, which aspect of coagulation is most likely affected in a 23-year-old man who presented with severe gum bleeding?\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n- The patient has bleeding from his gums while brushing his teeth for the past week, which is more severe than his previous episodes of gum bleeding.\n- His physical exam is normal, but his lab values show decreased Factor VIII activity and Ristocetin cofactor assay.\n- Factor VIII is a clotting factor that is important for the intrinsic pathway of coagulation, which is activated by damage to blood vessels.\n- The Ristocetin cofactor assay measures the ability of von Willebrand factor (vWF) to bind to platelets and initiate platelet aggregation, which is important for primary hemostasis.\n- Therefore, the most likely aspect of coagulation that is affected in this patient is the intrinsic pathway, which involves Factor VIII and vWF.\n\nAnswer: A) Factor IX",
