                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nThe patient's lab work indicates a decreased Factor VIII activity and decreased Ristocetin cofactor assay, which suggests a deficiency in von Willebrand factor (VWF). VWF is a glycoprotein that is involved in the adhesion of platelets to the site of injury and is a cofactor for Factor VIII. Therefore, the most likely aspect of coagulation that would be affected is Option B: Gp Ib.",
                        "answers": [
