                        "cot": "Let's think step by step like a medical expert. \n\nThe patient has chest pain that has been present for 4 hours. This is a new symptom, and it is important to find out if it is related to the myocardial infarction. \n\nThe patient's ECG is difficult to interpret. This means that it is not immediately clear if the chest pain is related to the myocardial infarction. \n\nThe most important laboratory test to determine if the chest pain is related to the myocardial infarction is the troponin T test. This test measures the level of troponin T, a protein that is released into the bloodstream when the heart is damaged. If the troponin T level is elevated, it is likely that the chest pain is related to the myocardial infarction.",
