                    {
                        "id": "d2f206a5-171f-4340-8474-096e19b7f3aa",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-10",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Plan:\n1. Assess the patient's symptoms and medical history.\n2. Check vital signs and perform a physical examination.\n3. Review the patient's ECG and laboratory test results.\n4. Determine which laboratory test would have the most diagnostic utility.\n\nAnswer:\nE) Troponin T would have the most diagnostic utility in this case. Troponin T is a cardiac-specific biomarker that is released into the bloodstream when there is damage to the heart muscle. An elevated troponin T level would indicate ongoing myocardial damage and would support the diagnosis of recurrent myocardial infarction. The other laboratory tests listed (alanine aminotransferase, alkaline phosphatase, creatine kinase (CK-MB), and lactate dehydrogenase) are not specific to cardiac damage and would not provide as much diagnostic information in this case.",
                        "answers": [
