                        "instruction": "qa-10",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Step 1: Understand the patient's history and current symptoms\n- The patient had an acute myocardial infarction (heart attack) 5 days ago and was treated with alteplase (a clot-busting drug).\n- He is now experiencing chest pain and left shoulder discomfort similar to his initial symptoms.\n\nStep 2: Consider the possible causes of the patient's current symptoms\n- Recurrence of myocardial infarction\n- Complications from the initial myocardial infarction\n- Other unrelated causes of chest pain\n\nStep 3: Evaluate the patient's vital signs and physical exam findings\n- Pulse: 86/min (slightly elevated)\n- Respiratory rate: 16/min (normal)\n- Blood pressure: 146/90 mm Hg (elevated)\n- Chest auscultation: no abnormal findings\n\nStep 4: Determine which laboratory test would be most useful in diagnosing the cause of the patient's symptoms\n- A) Alanine aminotransferase: primarily used to evaluate liver function, not relevant to this case\n- B) Alkaline phosphatase: primarily used to evaluate liver and bone disorders, not relevant to this case\n- C) Creatine kinase (CK-MB): a cardiac-specific enzyme that is elevated in myocardial infarction\n- D) Lactate dehydrogenase: a non-specific enzyme that can be elevated in many conditions, including myocardial infarction, but is less specific than CK-MB or troponin T\n- E) Troponin T: a cardiac-specific protein that is elevated in myocardial infarction and is considered the gold standard for diagnosing myocardial infarction\n\nAnswer: E) Troponin T",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "74a436ff-af07-4146-813a-c424fb520ee8",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-E",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "E) Troponin T, as it is a cardiac-specific protein that is elevated in myocardial infarction and is considered the gold standard for diagnosing myocardial infarction.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "E",
                                "correct_answer": false
                            }
                        ],
                        "author": "thoughtsource",
                        "date": "2023/04/12 22:45:57",
                        "api_service": "openai_chat",
