                    },
                    {
                        "id": "ea05ddef-dee1-447e-9f04-05857e8cbd3f",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-13",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Question: Which abnormal laboratory test result would be most useful for diagnosing the current condition of a 59-year-old man who has been experiencing chest pain for 4 hours on the 5th day of hospitalization for acute myocardial infarction, and has previously been treated with alteplase?\n\nStep 1: Identify the relevant information from the patient's history and symptoms.\n- 59-year-old man\n- Chest pain for 4 hours on the 5th day of hospitalization\n- Acute myocardial infarction\n- Treated with alteplase\n- Discomfort in chest and left shoulder\n- Pulse: 86/min, respiratory rate: 16/min, blood pressure: 146/90 mm Hg\n- No abnormal findings in chest auscultation\n- Difficult-to-interpret ECG\n\nStep 2: Analyze the possible diagnostic utility of each laboratory test.\nA) Alanine aminotransferase: This enzyme is primarily associated with liver function, and an abnormal result would not be particularly useful for diagnosing the patient's current condition.\nB) Alkaline phosphatase: This enzyme is associated with liver and bone disorders, and an abnormal result would not be particularly useful for diagnosing the patient's current condition.\nC) Creatine kinase (CK-MB): This enzyme is specific to heart muscle damage and is a marker for myocardial infarction. An abnormal result would be highly useful for diagnosing the patient's current condition.\nD) Lactate dehydrogenase: This enzyme is found in many tissues and is not specific to heart muscle damage. An abnormal result would not be particularly useful for diagnosing the patient's current condition.\nE) Troponin T: This protein is specific to heart muscle damage and is a marker for myocardial infarction. An abnormal result would be highly useful for diagnosing the patient's current condition.\n\nStep 3: Determine the most useful laboratory test for diagnosing the patient's current condition.\nBoth Creatine kinase (CK-MB) and Troponin T are markers for myocardial infarction and would be highly useful for diagnosing the patient's current condition. However, Troponin T is considered a more sensitive and specific marker for myocardial infarction than CK-MB. Therefore, an abnormal result of Troponin T (Option E) would have the most diagnostic utility in this case.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "5e08167f-3bf3-4fea-a924-d858c583940b",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-E",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "E) Troponin T.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "E",
                                "correct_answer": false
                            }
                        ],
                        "author": "thoughtsource",
                        "date": "2023/04/12 22:48:23",
