                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nThe correct answer is E. Troponin T is a protein found in the heart muscle. It is released into the bloodstream when the heart muscle is damaged. An elevated troponin T level is a sign of heart damage.\nA) Alanine aminotransferase is an enzyme found in the liver. It is released into the bloodstream when the liver is damaged. An elevated alanine aminotransferase level is a sign of liver damage.\nB) Alkaline phosphatase is an enzyme found in the liver and bones. It is released into the bloodstream when the liver or bones are damaged. An elevated alkaline phosphatase level is a sign of liver or bone damage.\nC) Creatine kinase (CK-MB) is an enzyme found in the heart muscle. It is released into the bloodstream when the heart muscle is damaged. An elevated creatine kinase (CK-MB) level is a sign of heart damage.\nD) Lactate dehydrogenase is an enzyme found in the liver and muscles. It is released into the bloodstream when the liver or muscles are damaged. An elevated lactate dehydrogenase level is a sign of liver or muscle damage.",
