                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nThe most diagnostic utility would be Creatine Kinase (CK-MB). This is because CK-MB is an enzyme that is released into the bloodstream when there is damage to the heart muscle, which is what is suspected in this case. An elevated CK-MB level would indicate that the patient is having a myocardial infarction, which is what the patient is suspected of having. Alanine aminotransferase, alkaline phosphatase, lactate dehydrogenase, and troponin T are all enzymes that are released into the bloodstream when there is damage to other organs, such as the liver, bones, and muscles, and would not be as useful in diagnosing a myocardial infarction. Therefore, the answer is C) Creatine Kinase (CK-MB).",
