                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nGiven the patient's symptoms and the fact that he was initially diagnosed with an ST-elevation myocardial infarction, the most diagnostic utility would be from a laboratory test of Troponin T. Troponin T is a protein found in the heart muscle and is released into the bloodstream when the heart muscle is damaged. An elevated level of Troponin T in the blood is a sign of a heart attack. Therefore, the laboratory test with the most diagnostic utility in this case would be Troponin T.",
