                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "C) Creatine kinase (CK-MB)\n\nCritique: The answer choice of creatine kinase (CK-MB) is a reasonable option, as it is a cardiac biomarker that can indicate myocardial damage. However, troponin T is a more specific and sensitive marker for myocardial injury and would be a better choice in this scenario.\n\nReconsidering other answer options:\nA) Alanine aminotransferase - This enzyme is primarily associated with liver function and would not be the most useful in diagnosing a cardiac issue.\nB) Alkaline phosphatase - This enzyme is associated with bone and liver function, not cardiac issues.\nD) Lactate dehydrogenase - This enzyme is found in many tissues and is not specific to the heart, making it less useful for diagnosing myocardial injury.\nE) Troponin T - This is a highly specific and sensitive marker for myocardial injury and would be the best choice for diagnosing the patient's current condition.\n\nFinal answer: E) Troponin T",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "6695cf6f-460f-4784-bfaa-ca49d47a175b",
