                        "cot": "Question: What is the most appropriate procedure for elective termination of pregnancy in a 25-year-old woman who has missed her menstrual cycle for 4 weeks, has a positive urine pregnancy test, and desires to discontinue the pregnancy?\n\nStep 1: Determine the gestational age of the pregnancy.\nThe patient has missed her menstrual cycle for 4 weeks, which means she is likely around 4-5 weeks pregnant.\n\nStep 2: Consider the available options for elective termination of pregnancy at this gestational age.\nA) Dilatation and evacuation (D&E) - typically used for pregnancies between 13-24 weeks.\nB) Oxytocin-induced labor - typically used for pregnancies beyond 24 weeks.\nC) Manual uterine aspiration - typically used for pregnancies up to 10 weeks.\nD) Dilatation and curettage (D & C) after vacuum evacuation - typically used for pregnancies up to 12-14 weeks.\nE) Oral mifepristone + misoprostol - typically used for pregnancies up to 10 weeks.\n\nStep 3: Choose the most appropriate option for this patient's gestational age.\nSince the patient is around 4-5 weeks pregnant, the most appropriate option for elective termination of pregnancy in this case is:\n\nE) Oral mifepristone + misoprostol",
