                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Professor, I am having trouble understanding which procedure would be the most appropriate for elective termination of pregnancy in this patient. Can you help me work through the options?\n\nProfessor: Of course! Let's go through each option step by step. First, let's consider option A, Dilatation and Evacuation (D&E). This procedure is typically performed in the second trimester of pregnancy. Since the patient is only 4 weeks into her pregnancy, this option would not be appropriate. \n\nStudent: Okay, that makes sense. What about option B, Oxytocin-induced labor?\n\nProfessor: Oxytocin-induced labor is generally used for medical termination of pregnancy in the second or third trimester, or for inducing labor in full-term pregnancies. Again, since the patient is only 4 weeks pregnant, this option would not be appropriate.\n\nStudent: I see. How about option C, Manual uterine aspiration?\n\nProfessor: Manual uterine aspiration is a procedure that can be used for early pregnancy termination, typically up to 10 weeks gestation. This could be a potential option for this patient, as she is only 4 weeks pregnant. \n\nStudent: Alright. What about option D, Dilatation and curettage (D & C) after vacuum evacuation?\n\nProfessor: Dilatation and curettage (D & C) after vacuum evacuation is another option for early pregnancy termination. However, it is generally considered more invasive and has a higher risk of complications compared to manual uterine aspiration. \n\nStudent: Okay, and finally, what about option E, Oral mifepristone + misoprostol?\n\nProfessor: Oral mifepristone and misoprostol is a medical abortion option that can be used up to 10 weeks gestation. This method is less invasive than surgical options and has a high success rate. \n\nStudent: So, considering all the options, which one would be the most appropriate for this patient?\n\nProfessor: Based on the patient's gestational age and the available options, the most appropriate procedure for elective termination of pregnancy in this patient would be option E, Oral mifepristone + misoprostol. This method is less invasive and has a high success rate for early pregnancy termination.\n\nStudent: Thank you, Professor! I understand the reasoning behind the answer now.",
