                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nThe most appropriate procedure for elective termination of pregnancy in this patient is Dilatation and Evacuation (D&E). This procedure is the most commonly used method for elective termination of pregnancy in the second trimester (13-24 weeks). It is a safe and effective method for terminating a pregnancy and is associated with fewer complications than other methods. D&E involves dilating the cervix and then using suction and forceps to remove the fetus and placenta from the uterus. This procedure is usually done under general anesthesia and can be completed in one visit. It is important to note that this procedure is not recommended for women who have had a previous cesarean section or other uterine surgery.",
