                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Plan:\n- Identify the risk factors associated with post-term pregnancy\n- Evaluate the options for induction of labor\n- Determine the potential complications for the fetus\n\nAnswer:\nThe correct answer is D) Meconium aspiration.\n\nExplanation:\nPost-term pregnancy (gestational age of 42 weeks or more) is associated with an increased risk of fetal and maternal complications. The risk factors for post-term pregnancy include nulliparity, male fetus, obesity, and a history of post-term pregnancy. In this case, the patient is gravida 3 and has a history of two post-term pregnancies.\n\nInduction of labor is recommended for post-term pregnancies to reduce the risk of fetal and maternal complications. The options for induction of labor include cervical ripening agents, such as prostaglandins, and oxytocin infusion.\n\nThe potential complications for the fetus in post-term pregnancy include meconium aspiration, fetal distress, macrosomia, and stillbirth. Meconium aspiration occurs when the fetus passes stool (meconium) into the amniotic fluid, which can be aspirated into the lungs and cause respiratory distress. This is the most common complication associated with post-term pregnancy and is the correct answer to the question.\n\nPolyhydramnios is an excessive amount of amniotic fluid, which can be associated with fetal anomalies and maternal diabetes. Acute respiratory distress syndrome is a severe lung condition that can occur in premature infants or as a complication of other medical conditions. Caudal regression syndrome is a rare congenital disorder that affects the development of the lower spine and legs. Placental abruption is a serious complication in which the placenta separates from the uterine wall before delivery, which can cause fetal distress and maternal hemorrhage. These complications are not specifically associated with post-term pregnancy.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "3f3b34ea-a270-4d89-9321-2fb981d8b23f",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-E",
