                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nProfessor: \"It sounds like this patient is experiencing anticholinergic toxicity. The drug that would most likely be administered to treat her symptoms is Atropine.\"\n\nStudent: \"What is anticholinergic toxicity?\"\n\nProfessor: \"Anticholinergic toxicity is a condition caused by the overstimulation of the parasympathetic nervous system. It can be caused by certain medications, plants, or other substances that block the action of acetylcholine, a neurotransmitter that helps regulate the body's involuntary functions.\"\n\nStudent: \"What are the symptoms of anticholinergic toxicity?\"\n\nProfessor: \"The symptoms of anticholinergic toxicity can include muscle spasms, blurred vision, dry mouth, and hallucinations, which is what this patient is experiencing. Other symptoms can include dry red skin, enlarged pupils, and difficulty urinating.\"\n\nStudent: \"What is Atropine used to treat?\"\n\nProfessor: \"Atropine is an anticholinergic drug that is used to treat anticholinergic toxicity. It works by blocking the action of acetylcholine, which helps to reduce the symptoms of anticholinergic toxicity.\"",
