kely in a 57-year-old patient.\n\nBased on the patient's symptoms, laboratory findings, and the potential additional findings, the most likely additional finding in this patient is B) Cutaneous xanthomas. This is because xanthomas can be associated with liver dysfunction, which is consistent with the patient's presentation.",
