                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Plan:\n1. Assess the patient's condition and the urgency of the situation.\n2. Speak with the patient's wife to understand her religious beliefs and reasons for refusing a blood transfusion.\n3. Review the patient's medical chart and the annotation indicating no blood transfusions for religious reasons.\n4. Consult with the hospital's ethics board to discuss the situation and potential options.\n5. Consider alternative treatments or procedures that may be available to avoid the need for a blood transfusion.\n6. Make a decision that prioritizes the patient's health and well-being while respecting their religious beliefs and wishes.\n\nAnswer: A) Administer a blood transfusion to save the patient's life. While it is important to respect the patient's religious beliefs and wishes, the priority in this situation is to save the patient's life. As a healthcare professional, it is our duty to provide the best possible care for our patients, and in this case, a blood transfusion is necessary to do so. It is important to have a conversation with the patient's wife and involve the hospital's ethics board to ensure that the decision is made with careful consideration and respect for the patient's beliefs.",
