                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Rephrased question: What should be done when a patient needs a blood transfusion to save their life, but their medical chart and spouse indicate that they cannot receive one for religious reasons?\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n1. The patient needs a blood transfusion to save their life.\n2. The patient's medical chart and spouse indicate that they cannot receive a blood transfusion for religious reasons.\n3. It is important to respect the patient's wishes and beliefs, but saving their life is the top priority.\n4. Administering a blood transfusion goes against the patient's wishes and beliefs, but it is necessary to save their life.\n5. Calling the ethics board of the hospital may be helpful, but it may delay the necessary treatment.\n6. Convincing the wife to administer a blood transfusion may not be possible or ethical.\n7. Refusing to treat the patient is not an option as it goes against the medical oath to save lives.\n\nAnswer: A) Administer a blood transfusion to save the patient's life.",
