                        "instruction": null,
                        "cot_trigger": "lievin-10",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Let's think step by step like a medical expert. \n\nThe null hypothesis is that mepolizumab has no effect on asthma exacerbations. The alternative hypothesis is that mepolizumab reduces asthma exacerbations. \n\nA type 1 error would occur if the null hypothesis were true but was rejected in error. In other words, if mepolizumab actually has no effect on asthma exacerbations, but the study found that it does, that would be a type 1 error. \n\nThe type 1 error rate is usually 0.1 or 0.2.",
