                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Rephrased question: What is a type 1 error and how would it affect the conclusions of the study described in the research abstract?\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n- A type 1 error occurs when the null hypothesis is true but is rejected in error.\n- In the context of this study, the null hypothesis would be that there is no difference in the rate of exacerbations between the treatment groups (mepolizumab and placebo).\n- If the authors had inadvertently encountered a type 1 error, it would mean that they had incorrectly rejected the null hypothesis and concluded that there was a significant difference in the rate of exacerbations between the treatment groups when there actually wasn't.\n- This would lead to a false positive result and the conclusions of the study would be invalid.\n\nAnswer: B) A type 1 error occurs when the null hypothesis is true but is rejected in error.",
