                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "B) A type 1 error occurs when the null hypothesis is true but is rejected in error.\n\nExplanation:\nA type 1 error, also known as an alpha (\u03b1) error, occurs when the null hypothesis (i.e., no significant difference between the study groups) is true, but the study results lead to its rejection. In this case, if the authors had encountered a type 1 error, it would mean that there is actually no significant difference in asthma exacerbations and markers of asthma control between the mepolizumab and placebo groups, despite the study results suggesting otherwise.",
