                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nStudent: What is a type 1 error?\n\nProfessor: A type 1 error occurs when the null hypothesis is false, yet is accepted in error. This means that the researchers have incorrectly concluded that there is no difference between the study groups when in fact there is a difference. This is also known as a false positive. The probability of a type 1 error is usually set at 0.05, which means that there is a 5% chance of incorrectly rejecting the null hypothesis.",
