                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\nFirst, it is important to note that the patient has poorly controlled hypertension, which is why the physician added another anti-hypertensive medication.\n\nSub-question 1: What are the most common classes of anti-hypertensive medications?\nAnswer: The most common classes of anti-hypertensive medications are diuretics, beta-blockers, calcium channel blockers, angiotensin-converting enzyme (ACE) inhibitors, and angiotensin receptor blockers (ARBs).\n\nSub-question 2: What are the most common side effects of anti-hypertensive medications?\nAnswer: The most common side effects of anti-hypertensive medications are dizziness, fatigue, headache, nausea, and lower extremity swelling.\n\nBased on the patient's symptoms and the side effects of anti-hypertensive medications, the likely medication prescribed to this patient is D) Hydrochlorthiazide, a diuretic.",
